From: Steve Statia <stevestatia@google.com>
Date: Wed, 6 May 2026 23:13:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] [Telephony] Secure contact URI access in Call Forwarding

Enforce caller permission checks on the contact URIs returned by the
contact picker in CdmaCallForwardOptions and GsmUmtsCallForwardOptions.

A malicious third-party application acting as a contact picker could
return a specially crafted Enterprise URI (e.g., pointing to a protected
work profile contact) that it does not have permission to access. Due to
insufficient verification, the Phone app would query and display this
contact, leading to a cross-profile data leak (Confused Deputy).

This change:
- Validates that the calling application has explicit read permission to
  the returned contact URI using ComponentCaller.
- Adds defensive null checks for the contact URI after retrieval to
  prevent NullPointerExceptions in ContentResolver.query.

Bug: 490916793
Test: atest TeleServiceRoboTests:ContactPermissionUtilsTest
